# Man-Hours Estimation Rule

Every file in this project must carry a man-hours estimate representing the equivalent senior-engineer effort to produce the file's **current final state** from scratch.

## On File Creation

Add a comment on the **very first line** of the new file:

- **Markdown (`.md`, `.mdc`):** `<!-- man_hours: X.X -->`
- **Python (`.py`):** `# man_hours: X.X`
- **YAML / TOML / Mako (`.yml`, `.yaml`, `.toml`, `.mako`):** `# man_hours: X.X`

Then add a matching entry in `audit/man_hours_registry.yml` under the `files:` key:

```yaml
  path/to/file.ext:
    hours: X.X
    category: "<category>"
```

## On File Edit

Update the `man_hours` value in the file's first-line comment **and** in `audit/man_hours_registry.yml` so both reflect the **total cumulative** effort to produce the file in its current state — not just the incremental delta from this edit.

## Category Mapping

Derive the category from the file path prefix:

| Path prefix / filename                                            | Category                  |
| ----------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------- |
| `requirements/`                                                   | Requirements & Analysis   |
| `architecture/`                                                   | Architecture & Design     |
| `src/`                                                            | Implementation            |
| `tests/`                                                          | Testing                   |
| `alembic/`                                                        | Database & Migrations     |
| `config/`, `docker-compose.yml`, `pyproject.toml`, `.env*`, `.cursor/` | Configuration & DevOps    |
| `sources/`                                                        | Research & Data Sources   |
| `experts/`                                                        | AI Prompts & Tooling      |
| `audit/`                                                          | Project Management & QA   |

If a file does not match any prefix, use "Other".

## Estimation Guidance

Estimate as a **senior engineer** working alone, including research, design thinking, implementation, self-review, and iteration — not just raw typing time.

| Example file                              | Typical range | Why                                                             |
| ----------------------------------------- | ------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Simple `__init__.py` (empty or re-exports) | 0.1–0.25 h   | Boilerplate only                                                |
| Configuration (`default.yml`, `pyproject.toml`) | 1–4 h     | Research dependencies, tune thresholds, cross-check docs        |
| Alembic migration (13 tables, enums, indexes) | 8–12 h     | Schema design, field types, constraints, testing                |
| Connector (`corine.py`, ~370 LOC, WFS protocol) | 12–16 h   | API research, protocol handling, ring analysis, error handling  |
| Requirements spec (`01_overview.md`, ~260 lines) | 20–40 h   | Domain research, stakeholder alignment, technology comparison   |
| Architecture spec (screening engine, ~150 lines) | 8–16 h    | Design decisions, interface contracts, traceability mapping     |
| Test file (~200 LOC, mocks + fixtures)    | 4–8 h         | Fixture design, edge cases, integration setup                   |
| Regulation map (`SSG-35_map.md`)          | 6–12 h        | Read full IAEA document, extract and structure key information  |
| Expert system prompt (~280 lines)         | 6–10 h        | Cross-reference entire codebase, synthesize integration specs   |

## Excluded Files

Do not add man-hours comments to:

- Generated / aggregated files (`agregated_requirements.md`, `agregated_architecture.md`)
- Files inside `.venv/`, `.git/`, `__pycache__/`
- The registry itself (`audit/man_hours_registry.yml`)
- The generated summary (`audit/man_hours_summary.md`)

## Regenerating the Summary

After updating estimates, run:

```bash
python src/scripts/man_hours_report.py
```

This reads `audit/man_hours_registry.yml` and writes `audit/man_hours_summary.md` with:

- Git-tracked LOC (excludes `venv_test`, `.venv`, caches; non-overlapping Python buckets)
- Markdown/YAML breakdowns and deduped repo totals
- Product counts (criteria, connectors, expert prompts)
- Indicative LLM token model (output / input / thinking) from character counts
- Optional measured tokens when `logs/llm/` response JSON exists locally
- **`cloc`** physical source analysis (`--vcs=git`): code / comment / blank by language and product area (requires `cloc` on PATH, e.g. `brew install cloc`)

Implementation: `src/scripts/man_hours_report.py`, `src/scripts/_man_hours_metrics.py`.
